# hugmesh-coturn-firewall — coturn public-TURN node-firewall convergence timer (60s).
#
# The TIMER half of the coturn public-reachability gate (the OpenRC oneshot
# renders the hugmesh_coturn_relay backstop + reconciles the firewalld runtime
# port set once at boot; this cron re-runs it every 60s so touching/deleting
# /etc/hugmesh/coturn-public on a LIVE relay node — or a firewalld restart
# resetting the runtime port set to the baked baseline — converges without a
# reboot). cronie reads /etc/cron.d — the same mechanism every other hugmesh
# reconcile timer uses.
#
# The reconcile is idempotent + FAIL-CLOSED: a render/apply error leaves the
# existing ruleset in place and logs here (stdout+stderr are captured, so cron
# never mails root).
#
# Field order: min hour dom month dow user command
* * * * * root /usr/sbin/hugmesh-coturn-firewall >> /var/log/hugmesh-coturn-firewall.log 2>&1
